mokata is built clean-room. Its methodology and prompt devices are reimplemented
in mokata's own terminology; mokata takes no dependency on, and imports no code
or text from, any other AI-assisted-coding methodology framework.

Third-party files shipped with `mokata ide` (vendored, served locally, never from a CDN)
live in src/mokata/ide/static/vendor/, each pinned by version and sha256 in VERSIONS.json
beside its licence file:
  - Cytoscape.js, cytoscape-fcose, layout-base, cose-base, cytoscape-dagre, @dagrejs/dagre (MIT)
  - markdown-it (MIT), with entities (BSD-2-Clause, Copyright (c) Felix Böhm) bundled in its build
  - mermaid (MIT), with the licence notices of its bundled dependencies kept in mermaid.min.js
